WEBVTT

01:51.421 --> 01:53.001
In 1014,

01:53.631 --> 01:54.631
York

01:54.711 --> 01:59.091
was controlled by the Vikings of Denmark,
led by King Sweyn.

01:59.931 --> 02:02.301
The land was used as a base

02:02.391 --> 02:05.931
for exporting slaves all over Europe.

02:06.021 --> 02:07.271
The Vikings served as

02:07.481 --> 02:11.061
slave traders.

02:13.321 --> 02:15.571
I know how you feel, boss.

02:16.441 --> 02:19.071
But we're not rich enough to free the slaves

02:19.151 --> 02:19.991
Reunion

02:20.071 --> 02:21.161
out of compassion.

02:22.491 --> 02:24.741
It's been 11 years already.

02:25.451 --> 02:28.211
Isn't it about time now?

02:30.371 --> 02:33.541
That day, without Thors,

02:33.631 --> 02:36.171
we wouldn't have gotten out of there alive.

02:37.881 --> 02:40.341
I must repay him for his help.

02:43.551 --> 02:45.471
Hurry! All of these over here!

02:45.561 --> 02:48.181
-Over there!
-Hurry! Go!

02:48.271 --> 02:49.231
What?

02:49.811 --> 02:50.981
Hey! You!

02:51.811 --> 02:54.691
You in the dirty cargo ship!
Get that ship out of the way!

02:56.111 --> 02:59.611
Hurry up! The first ship's almost here--

03:00.361 --> 03:01.781
Heave ho!

03:01.861 --> 03:04.951
Heave ho! Heave ho!

03:05.281 --> 03:08.831
Hurry up! A nobleman's ships

03:08.911 --> 03:10.711
are about to pull in along this pier!

03:10.831 --> 03:12.001
I got it.

03:16.591 --> 03:18.011
So, this is York.

03:19.421 --> 03:20.721
It's a big town.

03:21.301 --> 03:25.761
Yes. It's an old town that prospered
in the days of the Roman Empire.

03:26.681 --> 03:31.271
People and goods from both Northern Europe
and England all gather here.

03:32.441 --> 03:37.191
His Highness the king must be planning to
establish the capital of his new dynasty here.

03:37.901 --> 03:41.361
It's a good decision. I'd do the same thing.

03:44.411 --> 03:47.201
Come on! Who cares if they're nobility?

03:47.951 --> 03:49.791
Those guys are a pain. Damn.

03:50.961 --> 03:53.291
Hey, boss. Take care of the one on the stern.

03:58.501 --> 03:59.631
That man...

04:01.011 --> 04:03.341
That's right. It's definitely him.

04:04.131 --> 04:06.971
I'd never forget that face.

04:08.721 --> 04:13.441
Askeladd! The pirate who killed Thors!

04:14.141 --> 04:16.941
-Hey! Don't push!
-Who's ships are those?

04:17.021 --> 04:18.731
-Prince Canute's.
-What will you do?

04:19.571 --> 04:22.151
The king is going to strike at tomorrow's banquet.

04:22.361 --> 04:25.321
Well, about that...

04:26.451 --> 04:31.201
It's obvious that we're going to lose out
at the Imperial Council tomorrow.

04:32.001 --> 04:34.331
For example, he could give different territories

04:34.421 --> 04:37.211
to you and Thorkell to isolate you.

04:37.291 --> 04:40.251
He'd be giving you a reward,
but he'd also be giving you an order.

04:41.631 --> 04:45.261
If you refused, you'd be suspected
of harboring rebellious intentions.

04:45.721 --> 04:48.471
It's all up to the king what he wants to do with you.

04:49.261 --> 04:51.641
If he takes Thorkell from us, we're in trouble.

04:52.221 --> 04:54.271
True. We'd be in trouble.

04:55.601 --> 04:58.111
So... What's the plan?

05:01.731 --> 05:02.991
How about this?

05:03.401 --> 05:07.661
We could try exposing the secret
to the people around here.

05:07.781 --> 05:08.911
Exposing the secret?

05:09.071 --> 05:10.331
Which one is the prince?

05:10.411 --> 05:12.081
Isn't that him?

05:12.161 --> 05:13.701
Your Highness Canute.

05:16.001 --> 05:17.961
I mean that you're going

05:19.081 --> 05:21.301
to die here right now.

05:32.511 --> 05:34.481
He got shot!

05:35.311 --> 05:37.941
His Highness the Prince got shot!

05:38.151 --> 05:40.191
-Raise your shields!
-Where'd it come from?

05:40.271 --> 05:42.611
From the north bank! Find them!

05:43.821 --> 05:46.241
He was shot from this side? Unbelievable.

05:47.201 --> 05:48.741
What an easy job.

05:55.791 --> 05:57.081
Hey!

05:57.161 --> 05:58.501
What's happening?

05:58.921 --> 06:01.001
This is bad.

06:01.091 --> 06:03.381
We better not get involved in this.

06:03.551 --> 06:05.421
Hey! Where are you going, boss?

06:06.261 --> 06:08.131
It's him! He was there!

06:12.511 --> 06:13.601
What's wrong?

06:15.181 --> 06:16.811
Are you okay?

06:16.981 --> 06:18.561
You're bleeding!

06:32.871 --> 06:35.161
You wasted so much of my time.

06:54.561 --> 06:57.101
Hey! You bastards!

06:57.851 --> 06:59.561
What's going on?

06:59.641 --> 07:02.561
I bet you're the snipers!

07:03.481 --> 07:06.651
He's the sniper. It wasn't me. Here's the weapon.

07:07.861 --> 07:09.361
What's that?

07:09.531 --> 07:12.201
-Is it a bow?
-That's the weapon?

07:12.281 --> 07:14.371
Is he your friend?

07:14.451 --> 07:15.451
No, I--

07:15.531 --> 07:17.951
You can't fool us!

07:18.041 --> 07:20.501
You're just trying to blame everything on him

07:20.581 --> 07:22.421
and save yourself!

07:22.501 --> 07:23.961
I said it wasn't me!

07:24.131 --> 07:26.461
No! I can tell from your eyes!

07:26.551 --> 07:29.171
Your eyes are so murky.

07:29.261 --> 07:32.131
It's so obvious that you're a villain--

07:37.561 --> 07:39.221
Don't resist, you bastard!

07:39.311 --> 07:41.021
Wait! Wait! Wait!

07:41.981 --> 07:43.231
He's using a knife.

07:43.941 --> 07:45.771
He's small and he's young.

07:46.611 --> 07:48.691
Are you...

07:49.821 --> 07:51.571
Thorfinn Karlsefni?

07:51.651 --> 07:52.651
Thorfinn?

07:53.531 --> 07:54.621
Karlsefni?

07:55.491 --> 07:56.581
Who is he?

07:56.661 --> 07:58.411
You idiot! Don't you know who he is?

07:58.491 --> 08:02.331
He's the man who won a duel against
Thorkell the Tall with only two knives!

08:02.411 --> 08:04.001
What? No way!

08:04.881 --> 08:06.131
In that case, this is bad.

08:06.291 --> 08:08.381
He's one of His Highness's vassals.

08:08.461 --> 08:09.301
Seriously?

08:09.381 --> 08:11.261
Excuse me for a bit.

08:12.931 --> 08:13.881
You...

08:14.431 --> 08:15.641
Are you...?

08:16.641 --> 08:19.061
You're from Iceland, right?

08:21.771 --> 08:22.601
Your name

08:23.521 --> 08:26.191
is Thorfinn, son of Thors!

08:29.361 --> 08:30.231
You're...

08:31.071 --> 08:32.781
Leif.

08:38.951 --> 08:41.951
You're alive! I'm so glad.

08:42.411 --> 08:44.871
I'm so glad!

08:46.421 --> 08:47.711
Out of the way!

08:47.881 --> 08:49.211
Don't shake him, you idiot!

08:49.381 --> 08:50.211
Where was he hit?

08:50.301 --> 08:51.211
His chest. It's bad!

08:51.381 --> 08:52.971
Your Highness! Hold on!

08:53.131 --> 08:55.591
Your Highness! We're going to cut off your clothes.

09:09.731 --> 09:13.571
I had that feeling all along.

09:15.491 --> 09:17.991
His Highness is a woman!

09:18.071 --> 09:20.831
-This is big news!
-No way!

09:20.911 --> 09:22.081
You idiots.

09:24.121 --> 09:25.581
I'm right here.

09:27.871 --> 09:28.961
You're right.

09:32.551 --> 09:34.211
Why did you choose a woman?

09:34.461 --> 09:38.681
We couldn't find any male slaves who looked similar.

09:40.801 --> 09:41.721
Can you save her?

09:43.101 --> 09:45.931
No. Not with where she got shot.

09:46.021 --> 09:50.061
If there was poison on the arrow,
then she's probably already...

09:53.401 --> 09:54.821
I'm sorry.

09:59.491 --> 10:01.411
Take care of her.

10:01.871 --> 10:03.951
Do everything you can.

10:04.451 --> 10:05.291
Yes.

10:08.251 --> 10:10.041
Well, you know...

10:10.131 --> 10:13.301
Your precautions have paid off, Your Highness.

10:14.171 --> 10:18.341
It seems that there are people hiding here in York

10:18.431 --> 10:20.391
who want to do you harm.

10:24.141 --> 10:25.181
I see.

10:26.271 --> 10:27.981
You want to get revenge.

10:28.691 --> 10:32.271
Yes. I'm going to kill him, no matter what.

10:32.861 --> 10:35.821
With my father's dagger.

10:37.691 --> 10:39.911
He's all beaten up.

10:40.911 --> 10:44.161
A young child survived on the battlefield.

10:44.701 --> 10:47.121
I'm sure he's seen hell.

10:48.711 --> 10:50.421
No. I can't.

10:50.501 --> 10:52.171
In order to save this child,

10:52.251 --> 10:55.461
I have to forget these last 11 years.

10:56.591 --> 10:57.591
Leif.

10:59.011 --> 11:01.891
What's happening in Vinland right now?

11:03.551 --> 11:05.471
My father had wanted to go there.

11:06.391 --> 11:08.271
I dream about it sometimes too.

11:09.141 --> 11:11.061
Did you build a village already?

11:13.151 --> 11:16.861
Why aren't you asking me about your mother
and your sister, who you left behind?

11:17.861 --> 11:21.991
After you left, Helga's health got worse.

11:23.161 --> 11:25.281
Go see her, Thorfinn.

11:25.911 --> 11:27.831
It would make Helga feel better--

11:27.911 --> 11:30.581
I'm asking you about Vinland!

11:31.501 --> 11:34.081
Don't talk to me about things I didn't ask you!

11:34.711 --> 11:38.421
Hey. Hey! Where are you going? Thorfinn!

11:40.921 --> 11:43.051
Let's go home, Thorfinn.

11:43.141 --> 11:46.351
You've had enough, right? Let's go home together.

11:48.181 --> 11:49.221
Enough?

11:51.521 --> 11:53.311
You have no idea.

11:54.731 --> 11:56.521
You don't know anything about

11:56.611 --> 11:58.611
what I went through between that day and today.

11:59.191 --> 12:00.031
Right?

12:01.361 --> 12:02.901
As long as Askeladd

12:02.991 --> 12:06.741
is still alive, eating and shitting, it'll never be enough!

12:07.411 --> 12:09.241
It'll never be enough!

12:13.421 --> 12:15.631
How could this have happened?

12:16.591 --> 12:19.091
That cheerful young child.

12:26.801 --> 12:30.271
I'm going to stay in this town
until you change your mind!

12:31.731 --> 12:32.641
Thorfinn!

12:33.441 --> 12:35.191
Let's go home!

12:38.901 --> 12:40.531
Hey. Here's some booze.

12:42.611 --> 12:43.781
Thanks.

12:43.861 --> 12:46.991
Nice room, Bjorn. I'm jealous.

12:49.371 --> 12:52.541
This room is too small of a reward
for risking my life.

12:54.961 --> 13:00.801
By the way,
Atli said he wanted to apologize to you.

13:02.421 --> 13:06.301
I've got no hard feelings for anyone
who cut me on the battlefield.

13:07.801 --> 13:11.061
Thorfinn's the only one who holds a grudge about it.

13:13.891 --> 13:15.351
I'm okay. So go.

13:15.441 --> 13:17.271
It's time for you to make your evil plans.

13:18.731 --> 13:20.771
Yeah. See you later.

13:24.191 --> 13:25.201
Askeladd.

13:29.621 --> 13:32.411
How is your leg?

13:37.041 --> 13:39.331
Well, I've been hit by a lot of arrows.

13:39.921 --> 13:41.131
But, well...

13:42.301 --> 13:45.171
It's good enough for me to hold a sword.

13:46.971 --> 13:47.881
I see.

13:49.391 --> 13:50.601
Then tomorrow.

13:52.811 --> 13:53.851
Okay.

13:55.021 --> 13:55.851
Tomorrow.

14:01.821 --> 14:04.901
We've been outwitted, Floki.

14:06.241 --> 14:07.991
I apologize.

14:11.321 --> 14:14.331
Askeladd? He's doing well.

14:16.451 --> 14:20.001
He's laid a curse on this town.

14:24.591 --> 14:26.551
The prince got killed?

14:26.631 --> 14:28.841
No! It was a double.

14:30.761 --> 14:32.051
It's so dangerous out there.

14:32.141 --> 14:35.271
We can't sleep in peace at night.

14:39.271 --> 14:41.651
What I don't understand

14:41.731 --> 14:45.821
is why the assassin was targeting the prince?

14:45.901 --> 14:48.401
Well, he's an important person!

14:48.491 --> 14:50.321
Of course someone would want to kill him!

14:50.491 --> 14:54.621
But King Sweyn is here!

14:54.701 --> 14:57.251
If they were going to go after someone, it would be him!

14:57.331 --> 14:58.871
Oh, you're right.

14:58.961 --> 15:01.831
And there are two heirs.

15:01.921 --> 15:05.631
So the fact that they went after the younger brother
must mean that...

15:05.711 --> 15:06.761
You there!

15:07.711 --> 15:11.301
I have some interesting information regarding that.

15:13.641 --> 15:14.971
Well,

15:15.061 --> 15:17.771
it's only a rumor, after all.

15:19.101 --> 15:21.481
Only a rumor?

15:21.561 --> 15:23.231
That's perfect.

15:24.811 --> 15:26.731
It's better not to offer definite proof.

15:26.821 --> 15:29.941
We should leave the king with some room.

15:31.571 --> 15:34.371
So you're the one who hired the assassin?

15:34.451 --> 15:36.121
You performed a part in your own play?

15:36.831 --> 15:39.121
It was some good acting, right?

15:39.201 --> 15:42.081
Spreading rumors isn't enough.

15:42.711 --> 15:47.381
That acting made the rumor seem real.
That's how the rumor will spread.

15:48.671 --> 15:51.881
Everyone knows of the dispute over succession
within Denmark's royal family.

15:52.051 --> 15:55.181
Now, there's been an assassination attempt,
and the rumors will spread.

15:55.801 --> 15:57.011
Well then, everyone.

15:57.601 --> 16:01.101
How is this going to affect tomorrow's meeting?

16:01.391 --> 16:02.521
I see.

16:03.231 --> 16:06.651
He won't be able to issue any orders
that would put me at a disadvantage.

16:07.441 --> 16:08.611
That's right.

16:09.401 --> 16:11.491
If he took Thorkell away from you,

16:11.571 --> 16:15.031
or sent you to a warzone, it would only feed the rumors.

16:16.321 --> 16:18.411
The king depends on public favor.

16:18.911 --> 16:22.711
If he gets a bad reputation among the military,
he won't be able to ignore it.

16:23.871 --> 16:27.131
Especially if they found out he murdered his own child.

16:29.671 --> 16:32.091
You're so cunning.

16:32.171 --> 16:34.591
Where did you learn how to do it?

16:34.681 --> 16:38.101
Brute force isn't the only way to fight.

16:38.181 --> 16:39.511
Did you learn something new?

16:40.851 --> 16:42.811
The king might not strike

16:42.891 --> 16:44.941
for the time being.

16:45.851 --> 16:47.401
It's a good way to buy time.

16:48.981 --> 16:49.981
But

16:50.071 --> 16:53.241
I won't let you use a double for me ever again.

16:54.111 --> 16:56.701
Yes. I apologize.

16:58.951 --> 17:02.951
I'm so impressed, Askeladd!

17:03.041 --> 17:05.791
I feel like I have a force of ten thousand on my side!

17:06.501 --> 17:08.131
Thanks.

17:08.291 --> 17:11.381
Well, it looks like our discussion is wrapping up.

17:11.461 --> 17:13.471
I'm going to run some errands now.

17:14.261 --> 17:17.431
Wow! Having him here is so reassuring!

17:19.931 --> 17:20.761
Your Highness.

17:21.771 --> 17:24.351
You must not trust Gunnar.

17:25.021 --> 17:27.101
He's probably communicating with King Sweyn.

17:28.271 --> 17:31.111
Why do you think so? Tell me your reason.

17:31.271 --> 17:34.571
It's my gut feeling. But I'm sure about it.

17:34.651 --> 17:38.661
Then wasn't that bad just now?
He'll find out about what we were talking about.

17:38.741 --> 17:40.071
I don't care.

17:40.161 --> 17:42.491
I've only talked about things that are superfluous.

17:43.291 --> 17:47.171
If Gunnar is on their side, then he's going to
tell them tonight about what he just heard.

17:47.251 --> 17:50.501
I asked Thorfinn to follow him to make sure.

17:51.541 --> 17:53.881
What are you going to do if Gunnar is a spy?

17:54.551 --> 17:55.671
Are you going to kill him?

17:58.051 --> 17:59.471
Let him work.

18:00.681 --> 18:04.721
We'll use him to tell the king

18:04.931 --> 18:06.981
that we don't want a short-term battle.

18:07.691 --> 18:10.691
If he hears it from his spy, he'll believe it, and relax.

18:11.441 --> 18:15.531
In order to avoid conflict for now, it's necessary to have
an understanding from both sides.

18:16.651 --> 18:19.451
My plan is complete now.

18:24.201 --> 18:26.331
You're unbelievable.

18:27.541 --> 18:31.711
I'm looking forward to seeing
the king's reaction tomorrow.

18:40.221 --> 18:41.511
That's the king's house.

18:41.851 --> 18:42.931
Now, we know for sure.

18:48.021 --> 18:50.901
Everyone's obsessed with deceiving each other.

18:50.981 --> 18:53.111
Is that what a warrior is supposed to do?

18:54.191 --> 18:55.571
There's only one thing

18:56.441 --> 18:57.281
I'm supposed to do.

19:06.451 --> 19:09.831
Do we really have to do this before the Imperial Council,

19:09.911 --> 19:11.371
Thorfinn?

19:17.171 --> 19:20.341
Wouldn't it be better to wait
until your right arm heals?

19:22.341 --> 19:25.761
Well, I'm fine with it either way.

19:25.851 --> 19:27.851
I shall be the witness.

19:28.931 --> 19:31.481
The duel is over when I tell you to stop.

19:32.061 --> 19:33.151
You both agree with that?

19:34.271 --> 19:35.691
Fine with me.

19:36.071 --> 19:38.691
But please wait a moment, Your Highness.

19:39.861 --> 19:42.321
I have a previous engagement.

19:42.411 --> 19:43.621
I will return later.

19:53.081 --> 19:55.541
Sorry, Thorfinn.

19:56.501 --> 19:57.801
We'll be done soon.

20:02.471 --> 20:05.301
Understood. Begin.

20:26.741 --> 20:27.781
Askeladd.

20:29.161 --> 20:31.501
You're strong and smart.

20:32.911 --> 20:34.831
I look up to you.

20:37.171 --> 20:38.211
Even though

20:38.881 --> 20:41.881
you hate me from the bottom of your heart.

20:45.221 --> 20:46.931
Hey, Askeladd.

20:48.101 --> 20:49.561
I'm not the only one.

20:50.561 --> 20:51.681
You hated

20:51.771 --> 20:53.771
our friends who died...

20:54.601 --> 20:56.691
and even yourself.

21:01.071 --> 21:02.941
Aren't you lonely?

21:04.701 --> 21:06.411
Rejecting everything

21:06.491 --> 21:08.491
like that?

21:11.041 --> 21:12.161
I...

21:13.081 --> 21:14.211
wanted...

21:17.211 --> 21:18.291
Wanted...

21:20.211 --> 21:22.511
to be friends with you.

21:48.491 --> 21:51.201
Sorry! I missed the vital spot! I'll put you at ease.

21:51.281 --> 21:53.581
Askeladd...

21:55.411 --> 21:57.791
I wanted to be friends with you...

22:04.301 --> 22:05.721
Yeah. Bjorn...

22:07.261 --> 22:08.221
You're

22:09.761 --> 22:11.431
my only

22:12.681 --> 22:13.721
friend.

22:28.451 --> 22:30.531
Send me off.

22:56.931 --> 23:00.481
Well, then. Sorry to keep you waiting, kid.

23:01.351 --> 23:02.231
Come.

23:07.691 --> 23:08.991
I'll play with you.
